{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1299119-outer-sensh-i-mean-sidereals","id":1299119,"title":"Outer Sensh- I mean Sidereals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-23T20:21:15-07:00","id":1299119,"title":"Outer Sensh- I mean Sidereals?","content":"So I\u2019ve gotten to thinking about coming up with my own concepts in the deep quagmire of my mind, and I love the Sidereals quite a lot.<br /> <br /> However, I\u2019ve found that the outer planets, some of the best boys of our solar system, are unfortunately lacking in representation just like they are in many forms of traditional astrology.<br /> <br /> What can I do to rectify this? Think!<br /> <br /> What I dreamed up was the three outers, being Uranus, Neptune (best boi alert), and Pluto are three brothers who exist far beyond the Five Maidens. They function similarly to the regular Sidereals, but are far fewer in number. They are highly concerned with keeping creation in tact but, unlike their own inner brethren, they are not so bound by factions and the great prophecy. Granted, these ideas are all very alpha of alpha, but hopefully someone will get the gist.<br /> <br /> Taking the actual brothers into account, I like to think of them as the \u2018older brothers\u2019 to the five maidens, similar in the astrological concept that they outer planets are higher octaves of the inner planets. Uranus is the big brother to Mercury, Neptune is the big brother to Venus and Jupiter, and Pluto is the big brother to Mars and Saturn.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t really thought of their place in the world, but maybe they are something of a contingency plan in case everything goes tits up in creation.<br /> <br /> That being said, the actual outer Sidereals are actually rather mobile through creation, though often times work solo or in very small groups. <br /> <br /> For the actual castes based around the planets, I have come up with some fun ideas of their culture and abilities, but mostly for the neptunian variety.<br /> <br /> In astrology, Neptune (names for the Roman god of the sea) is a planet of dreams, illusion, romance, strong emotions, mysticism, and all things psychedelic. I\u2019d love to get into the more esoteric aspects of his correspondences, but it\u2019s getting late. The amount of charms and abilities one could think of are mind numbingly large when taking just these few themes into account.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll write more later on (if anyone is truly interested).<br /> <br /> I\u2019d love to hear feedback and have other people add on to these concepts as well. I hope this sparks some people\u2019s creativity~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T23:52:56-07:00","id":1299144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I\u2019ve found that the outer planets, some of the best boys of our solar system, are unfortunately lacking in representation just like they are in many forms of traditional astrology. </div> </div> </div>Probably because the outer planets aren't visible to the ancient Greek/Roman which is where the Incarnae takes inspiration from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The name &quot;planet&quot; comes from the Greek term \u03c0\u03bb\u03b1\u03bd\u03ae\u03c4\u03b7\u03c2 (<i>plan\u0113t\u0113s</i>), meaning &quot;wanderer&quot;, as ancient astronomers noted how certain lights moved across the sky in relation to the other stars. Five planets can be seen with the naked eye: Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn, the Greek names being Hermes, Aphrodite, Ares, Zeus and Cronus. Sometimes the luminaries, the Sun and Moon, are added to the list of naked eye planets to make a total of seven. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T03:54:06-07:00","id":1299164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1299119-outer-sensh-i-mean-sidereals?p=1299144#post1299144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because the outer planets aren't visible to the ancient Greek/Roman which is where the Incarnae takes inspiration from.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it\u2019s exactly why I mentioned these very things. In fact, I brought up the themes of being few in number and working alone.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m quite familiar with astrology (traditional and modern and a bit of Vedic as well), so that\u2019s where I\u2019m taking most of my inspiration from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T22:18:31-07:00","id":1299520,"title":"","content":"I love the idea, I've run ahead some of my own thoughts:<br /> They even come with their own nemesis. Planet X, the mythical planet that doesn't exist. Probably. <br /> <br /> No one has seen the oldest sibling. Ancient records from before state there were only the 8 siblings. And yet, every now and then, an astrological recording is off. Way off. And easily explained by the movement of another brother or sister. But even wen calculated by all of heaven's astrologers, the loom does not show such a being. <br /> Young Sidereals whisper that these are ghost stories meant to frighten initiates. But the elders note that there are many mysteries hidden in creation, and many influences on creation's future have veered sharply off course without any effort by the enemies of heaven. While the Magicians under Neptune's sway peer deep within the loom, sometimes they say that something blinks back at them. If the outer guardians protect creation against the errors within itself, as the inner guardians protect against it outward enemies, then certainly it is not unreasonable to think that they defend not against random errors and chance failures, but the machinations of the oldest of the siblings.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4959-drdog","name":"DrDog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T06:56:49-07:00","id":1299583,"title":"","content":"Another possible direction to take this is that Uranus, Neptune, and Pluto were felled during the Divine Revolution, and their Chosen ceased to rise. The Maidens of Destiny had foreseen this cost and went forward anyways, although they knew the price would be dear and bitter.<br /> <br /> For long years, it was assumed that never again would their Chosen be seen again. Until Rakan Thulio found the Tomb of Fallen Stars in distant Zen-Mu, and beckoned forth Exaltations grown strange and warped from their long absence- weaving their own destinies, apart from those of the Loom...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T09:23:02-07:00","id":1299620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1299119-outer-sensh-i-mean-sidereals?p=1299583#post1299583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possible direction to take this is that Uranus, Neptune, and Pluto were felled during the Divine Revolution, and their Chosen ceased to rise. The Maidens of Destiny had foreseen this cost and went forward anyways, although they knew the price would be dear and bitter.<br /> <br /> For long years, it was assumed that never again would their Chosen be seen again. Until Rakan Thulio found the Tomb of Fallen Stars in distant Zen-Mu, and beckoned forth Exaltations grown strange and warped from their long absence- weaving their own destinies, apart from those of the Loom...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an amazing take on the premise from the OP. Love it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> May have to develop some game threads based on this now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}